  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to the decrease of mortality and morbidity related to malaria in Guinea-Bissau - Guinea-Bissau (01-Apr-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guinea-Bissau, Malaria, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Guinea-Bissau)This program has the following goals: Contribute to reducing malaria-related morbidity and mortality in Guinea-Bissau. The objectives of this program are: By the end of 2017, at least 70 percent of pregnant women will be receiving a minimum of three doses of IPT under direct observation.  By the end of 2017, at least 85 percent of children aged 3-59 months will be covered by SMC in the target areas.  By the end of 2017, at least 90 percent of malaria cases will be correctly managed in health care facilities.  By the end of 2017, at least 95 percent of the population will be sleeping under an LLIN.  Strengthen the M&amp;E system.  Strengthen the management and coordination of the NMCP by the end of 2017</narrative>
  </description>
